    "body": "NaN differences never exceed a tolerance, so GRPO validation silently accepts invalid samples. Reject nonfinite golden and current values before computing differences.\n\nValidation: five baseline regressions fail; six focused CPU tests pass with the fix. Black, isort and Ruff passed. GPU training was not run.\n\nReview requested: @NVIDIA/mcore-oncall. This PR is ready for review with CPU regression evidence above. Upstream runner validation remains subject to NVIDIA contributor vetting.\n",
    "changed_files": 2,
